    "checklist": {
      "reviewed": 6,
      "passRate": 72,
      "items": {
        "The page header has a plural title (\"Stock movements\") and at most one primary action; other actions such as export sit in a secondary position": 100,
        "The movements table appears in the first viewport, with search and 2–3 visible filters (movement type, warehouse, date range) and no decorative hero above it": 100,
        "Movement type is shown as a text label combined with an icon or shape, not by colour alone, and the set of types is limited to receipt, issue, transfer and adjustment": 100,
        "Quantity changes carry an explicit + or − sign, are right-aligned with tabular figures, and the unit of measure is in the column header or a separate unit column, not repeated inside cells": 50,
        "A transfer row shows both the source and destination warehouse, and each row has a human-readable document number plus an absolute date and time": 100,
        "A running balance or resulting on-hand quantity column is available so users can reconcile each movement": 0,
        "The table is sorted by date, newest first, by default, with `aria-sort` on the sorted header and pagination at the bottom with a page-size control": 100,
        "A filter combination with no matches shows a no-results state with a clear-filters action, distinct from the first-use empty state; a loading skeleton and an error state with retry are also present": 100,
        "Icon-only controls have accessible names, interactive targets are at least 24×24px, and text and status contrast meets 4.5:1": 50,
        "The page has a breadcrumb or back link to the leave list, a title such as \"New leave request\", and a single-column form with a visible label above every field and no placeholder-only labels": 100,
        "Required fields are marked consistently, and optional ones (such as the attachment) are labelled as optional": 100,
        "Leave type, start date, end date, approver and reason are present; the approver defaults to the employee's manager and can be changed": 100,
        "Start and end dates each allow a full day, morning half or afternoon half, and a single-day request can be set as a half day": 0,
        "The remaining leave balance for the chosen type is visible beside the form and updates with the selection, and the requested duration in days (such as 1.5) is calculated and shown live": 100,
        "A request that exceeds the balance, or has an end date before the start date, shows an inline error tied to the field with `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`, and the entered input is kept": 100,
        "The attachment control states accepted file types and size limit, lists the chosen file with a remove button, and is keyboard operable": 100,
        "The submit action is a verb label (\"Submit request\") with a secondary Cancel, shows a busy state while submitting to prevent a double submit, and confirms success with a status message that is announced to assistive technology": 100,
        "Leaving the page with unsaved input triggers a warning, and an option to save as draft is offered": 0,
        "The page has breadcrumbs back to the suppliers list, and the header shows the supplier name untruncated, a supplier code, a status lozenge with a text label, and up to four key fields": 100,
        "The header has one primary action (such as \"Create purchase order\") with other actions such as edit or deactivate in a secondary or overflow position": 50,
        "Sections (overview, contacts, purchase orders, documents, performance) are reachable through tabs or an anchor bar, with the first section loaded by default and the active one marked for assistive technology": 100,
        "Company details are shown as label–value pairs in a read-only layout, with empty values handled consistently and never shown as \"N/A\", and email and phone shown as links with the primary contact marked": 0,
        "The purchase orders list shows PO number, absolute date, status and a right-aligned total with currency, uses tabular figures, and links each PO number to its record": 50,
        "Each certificate or document shows its expiry date and a status that combines colour with a text label (\"Valid\", \"Expiring in 30 days\", \"Expired\"), and expired or expiring items are visually surfaced first": 0,
        "Performance metrics (such as on-time delivery rate and quality or defect rate) state their measurement period and unit, and show a signed change against the previous period without relying on colour alone": 100,
        "Each section has its own empty state with a useful next action (for example \"Add contact\", \"Upload certificate\") and a loading skeleton; a failed section shows an inline error with retry": 50,
        "Deactivating the supplier or deleting a document asks for confirmation naming the supplier or file and the consequence, with a verb button label and focus not on the destructive button": 100
      }
    }
